1398:
1399:	    The repair is owed by the LANGUAGE at both widths; only one was returning
1400:	    a wrong value on this host.  `1U' defends 31 and the guard defends 32 --
1401:	    but a guest-VALUE probe cannot establish that, because `1 << 31' and
1402:	    `1U << 31' yield the SAME mask after the `- 1'.  No row can kill a
1403:	    `1U' -> `1' regression; UBSAN or a source pin can.
1404:
1405:	    The SHAPE comes from `cpu_m88k_instr.c's X(clr)/X(set), but the analogy
1406:	    needs care and an earlier draft ran the two together: there `w == 0'
1407:	    ENCODES full width and the guard selects the full-width mask instead of
1408:	    zero.  **It is not defending against a shift by 32 -- m88k's encoded
